description:
Implement a 32-bit multiplier circuit that performs a series of arithmetic operations on a single 32-bit input. It effectively calculates the product of the input value by 32, subtracts a quarter of the input value, executes a combination of shifts, and finally outputs a scaled result. The primary design utilizes left shifts and basic arithmetic to achieve the multiplication, highlighting a combinational logic approach to achieve the final output based on the input.
