description:
Design a half adder circuit that computes the sum and carry-out for two single-bit binary inputs, a and b. The sum output is generated using a combination of NAND gates to effectively perform the XOR function, while the carry-out output is derived using NAND gates to implement the AND function. This module performs the basic arithmetic operation needed in digital circuits for adding two bits.
module top_module(
    input a, b,
    output cout, sum
);

code:
module top_module(
    input a, b,
    output cout, sum
);wire w1, w2, w3;

  // Implementing the sum output using NAND gates
  nand(w1, a, b);
  nand(w2, a, w1);
  nand(w3, b, w1);
  nand(sum, w2, w3);

  // Implementing the carry-out output using NAND gates
  nand(cout, w1, w1);

endmodule

